→- If a field has no relevant content, use an empty array [] or null as appropriate.\n    32→- Do not invent information that is not visible or strongly implied by the menu.\n    33→- Output only the JSON array, nothing else.\n    34→\"\"\".strip()\n    35→\n    36→\n    37→def extract_menu(image_bytes: bytes, mime_type: str = \"image/jpeg\") -> list[dict]:\n    38→    \"\"\"\n    39→    Base64-encode *image_bytes*, send to GPT-4o-mini vision, and return a list\n    40→    of menu-item dicts.  Each dict contains:\n    41→        name, description, common_ingredients,\n    42→        obscure_ingredient_notes, allergy_warnings, dietary_flags\n    43→    \"\"\"\n    44→    b64 = base64.b64encode(image_bytes).decode(\"utf-8\")\n    45→    data_url = f\"data:{mime_type};base64,{b64}\"\n    46→\n    47→    response = _get_client().chat.completions.create(\n    48→        model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n    49→        messages=[\n    50→            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": _SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n    51→            {\n    52→                \"role\": \"user\",\n    53→                \"content\": [\n    54→                    {\n    55→                        \"type\": \"image_url\",\n    56→                        \"image_url\": {\"url\": data_url, \"detail\": \"high\"},\n    57→                    },\n    58→                    {\n    59→                        \"type\": \"text\",\n    60→                        \"text\": \"Extract all menu items from this image and return the JSON array.\",\n    61→                    },\n    62→                ],\n    63→            },\n    64→        ],\n    65→        max_tokens=4096,\n    66→        temperature=0,\n    67→    )\n    68→\n    69→    raw = response.choices[0].message.content or \"\"\n    70→    raw = raw.strip()\n    71→\n    72→    # Strip accidental markdown code fences (```json … ```)\n    73→    raw = re.sub(r\"^```(?:json)?\\s*\", \"\", raw)\n    74→    raw = re.sub(r\"\\s*```$\", \"\", raw)\n    75→\n    76→    items: list[dict] = json.loads(raw)\n    77→    return items\n    78→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"uuid":"3b677732-27d2-4540-b2a8-849a07cbefa5","timestamp":"2026-04-25T04:35:21.482Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/starnaphie/Downloads/02-doc-scanner-steef/backend/extractor.py","content":"import base64\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\n\nfrom openai import OpenAI\n\n_client: OpenAI | None = None\n\n\ndef _get_client() -> OpenAI:\n    global _client\n    if _client is None:\n        _client = OpenAI(api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"))\n    return _client\n\n_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"\nYou are a professional menu analyst. Given an image of a restaurant menu, extract every dish or drink item you can identify.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON array (no markdown, no code fences). Each element must be an object with these keys:\n\n- name (string): the item's name as printed\n- description (string | null): the item's description as printed, or null if absent\n- common_ingredients (array of strings): well-known ingredients a typical person would recognise (e.g. chicken, pasta, tomato)\n- obscure_ingredient_notes (array of strings): unusual, regional, or technical ingredients that may be unfamiliar, with a brief plain-language note for each (e.g. \"guanciale – cured pork cheek, similar to bacon\")\n- allergy_warnings (array of strings): any allergens mentioned or strongly implied (e.g. gluten, nuts, dairy, shellfish, eggs, soy, sesame)\n- dietary_flags (array of strings): applicable dietary labels (e.g. vegan, vegetarian, gluten-free, halal, kosher, spicy)\n\nRules:\n- Include every distinct item — starters, mains, desserts, drinks, sides, specials.\n- If a field has no relevant content, use an empty array [] or null as appropriate.\n- Do not invent information that is not visible or strongly implied by the menu.\n- Output only the JSON array, nothing else.\n\"\"\".strip()\n\n\ndef extract_menu(image_bytes: bytes, mime_type: str = \"image/jpeg\") -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Base64-encode *image_bytes*, send to GPT-4o-mini vision, and return a list\n    of menu-item dicts.  Each dict contains:\n        name, description, common_ingredients,\n        obscure_ingredient_notes, allergy_warnings, dietary_flags\n    \"\"\"\n    b64 = base64.b64encode(image_bytes).decode(\"utf-8\")\n    data_url = f\"data:{mime_type};base64,{b64}\"\n\n    response = _get_client().chat.completions.create(\n        model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n        messages=[\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": _SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n            {\n                \"role\": \"user\",\n                \"content\": [\n                    {\n                        \"type\": \"image_url\",\n                        \"image_url\": {\"url\": data_url, \"detail\": \"high\"},\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"type\": \"text\",\n                        \"text\": \"Extract all menu items from this image and return the JSON array.\",\n                    },\n                ],\n            },\n        ],\n        max_tokens=4096,\n        temperature=0,\n    )\n\n    raw = response.choices[0].message.content or \"\"\n    raw = raw.strip()\n\n    # Strip accidental markdown code fences (```json … ```)\n    raw = re.sub(r\"^```(?:json)?\\s*\", \"\", raw)\n    raw = re.sub(r\"\\s*```$\", \"\", raw)\n\n    items: list[dict] = json.loads(raw)\n    return items\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1714be33-2a70-4622-b65f-ec6dc77f0d19"}
